  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), the page state: `reho.st` image fetched cookie-less with and without `Referer: https://forum.hardware.fr/`; one `http://`-only image host of `R20`/`R21`/`R22a` requested over `https`\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: `reho.st` image fetched cookie-less with and without `Referer: https://forum.hardware.fr/`; one `http://`-only image host of `R20`/`R21`/`R22a` requested over `https`\n\nNote: settles HFR-PROTOCOL §7 E26 and the `http`-only hosts of the LOT-071 (#95) decision D-071-1; plain GETs, no account, no upload\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it (LOT-002 (#39)..005 tooling); one PR per batch of captures; the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-056 (#82), LOT-071 (#95), LOT-083 (#101)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\n`docs/LOTS.md` \"Capture backlog (Mac)\", copied from the frozen old issue [francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#98](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/98).\n",
